Nightjar release notices
========================

Nightjar is one server binary. This notice names the runtime components that
Nightjar ships and points to the full license and notice material. It records
publisher-declared license metadata. It is not legal advice and not an audit of
file-level copyright notices.

Shipped in the Nightjar server binary and image
-----------------------------------------------

- Nightjar server binary and embedded web UI, project version 0.0.1, licensed
  GPL-3.0-only. The full license text is in LICENSE. The source is the Nightjar
  repository; the release/tag URL is supplied at publication (docs/RELEASE.md).
- Rust dependencies locked in server/Cargo.lock. Their publisher-declared
  license expressions and the generated notice are in notices/THIRD-PARTY.md;
  the committed expression map is notices/rust-licenses.json. The lockfile
  coverage includes target-specific and build dependencies, whether or not a
  particular release binary contains their code.
- Bundled SQLite (public domain), compiled by libsqlite3-sys with the bundled
  feature.
- hls.js 1.6.16 (Apache-2.0), bundled into the embedded web assets. The notice
  is notices/hls.js-1.6.16.txt and the license text is notices/Apache-2.0.txt.

Shipped in the Nightjar Linux image as external Debian packages
---------------------------------------------------------------

These are separate executables and shared libraries, not linked into the server
binary. The image keeps their installed Debian copyright files under
/usr/share/doc/nightjar/debian/.

- ffmpeg and ffprobe, Debian package ffmpeg 7:7.1.5-0+deb13u1, GPL-2+.
- ca-certificates 20250419, GPL-2+ packaging and MPL-2.0 CA data.
- intel-media-va-driver-non-free 25.2.3+ds1-1, Expat and BSD-3-clause
  components. Debian places this package in non-free because it carries Intel
  media kernels without source; its copyright file records that.
- libmfx-gen1.2 25.1.4-1, MIT.
- mesa-va-drivers 25.0.7-2+deb13u1, MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, SGI and Khronos
  components.
- i965-va-driver 2.4.1+dfsg1-2, Expat, Apache-2.0, EPL-1.0 and GPL-2+
  components.

The exact Debian source package, version and the Debian Snapshot retrieval
route are in docs/RELEASE.md.
